g
, 30 min), and the supernatant was subjected to immobilized metal affinity chromatography using a 1 mL Ni-NTA agarose column (QIAGEN, 30210) equilibrated with binding buffer. The protein was eluted with a buffer containing 20 mM Tris-HCl, 500 mM NaCl, and 300 mM imidazole at pH 8.5. The eluted protein was further purified by size-exclusion chromatography employing a 26/60 Superdex75 column equilibrated with a buffer containing 20 mM HEPES and 300 mM NaCl at pH 7.5. To produce the protein containing SeMet,
E. coli
